# 🎓 Student Placement Predictor

A Machine Learning–based web application that predicts whether a student is likely to be **Placed or Not Placed** based on academic performance and other relevant student attributes.

---

## 📌 Project Overview

Student placement prediction can help educational institutions and students understand the factors that may influence placement outcomes.

In this project, a **Logistic Regression classification model** is trained on student-related data. After training, the model is integrated into a **Streamlit web application**, where users can enter student information and receive a placement prediction.

---

## 🎯 Objective

The main objectives of this project are to:

* Build a Machine Learning model for student placement prediction.
* Use Logistic Regression for binary classification.
* Preprocess student-related data before model training.
* Evaluate the performance of the trained model.
* Save the trained model using Python's `pickle` module.
* Develop an interactive web interface using Streamlit.
* Allow users to enter student information and receive real-time predictions.

---

